This is Hidden Brain. I'm Shankar Vedanta. In February 2024, two German tourists visited Australia. During one section of their trip in Queensland, they turned off the main road on the advice of Google Maps. They figured that the road up ahead was closed because of a rising river and the detour would take them to their destination. As one of them put it later, they trusted the map. We decided, okay, let's follow Kulmer, because Kulmer knows maybe more than we know.
这里是《隐藏的大脑》。我是尚卡尔·韦丹塔。2024年2月，两名德国游客游览了澳大利亚。在昆士兰州的一段行程中，他们听从了谷歌地图的建议，驶离了主路。他们觉得前方道路因河水上涨而封闭，走这条绕路可以到达目的地。正如其中一人后来所说，他们信任这个地图。我们决定，好吧，那就跟着库尔默走，因为库尔默可能比我们知道得更多。

