her parents imagined. She and Norm's father fought. I remember growing up in a period where there would be calm, but then also really stormy periods where my parents are fighting a lot. Ultimately, that led to their divorce right around the time I left for university. By the time I was done, my undergraduate days, my parents had completely split and my mother was living on her own. This was a catastrophic change in the narrative that she expected for herself. Talk about that. I mean, she was raised with the notion that if she was a good daughter, a good wife, a good mother, that was the responsibility she had, and in turn, she would be looked after, she would have security, she would have stability. And in some ways, she had done her part, but life had massive disruption of the story she expected for herself
